From: Li Guan <guanli.oerv@isrc.iscas.ac.cn>
Subject: [PATCH] test: keep socket state queries pending on loopback

The socket-state delivery tests send queries to TEST-NET-1 and expect them
to remain pending. Without an external route, sending fails immediately
and the query completes before cancellation or destruction is tested.

Use the existing mock server on an ephemeral loopback port and leave it
unserviced. This keeps the query pending while retaining all socket-close
notification assertions.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Reference: https://github.com/c-ares/c-ares/blob/v1.34.9/test/ares-test-mock.cc
Signed-off-by: Li Guan <guanli.oerv@isrc.iscas.ac.cn>
---
--- a/test/ares-test-mock.cc
+++ b/test/ares-test-mock.cc
@@ -3997,6 +3997,8 @@
 
 class SockStateDeliveryTest : public LibraryTest {
 protected:
+  MockServer server_{AF_INET, 0};
+
   void OpenConnection(ares_channel_t **chan, SockStateRecordData *data,
                       QueryResult *result)
   {
@@ -4008,9 +4010,10 @@
     ASSERT_EQ(ARES_SUCCESS,
               ares_init_options(chan, &opts, ARES_OPT_SOCK_STATE_CB));
     ASSERT_NE(nullptr, *chan);
-    /* TEST-NET-1, guaranteed not to answer, so the socket is still open when
-     * the call under test runs. */
-    ASSERT_EQ(ARES_SUCCESS, ares_set_servers_csv(*chan, "192.0.2.1:53"));
+    /* Keep the query pending without requiring a route outside loopback. */
+    std::stringstream server;
+    server << "127.0.0.1:" << server_.udpport();
+    ASSERT_EQ(ARES_SUCCESS, ares_set_servers_csv(*chan, server.str().c_str()));
 
     ares_query_dnsrec(*chan, "www.google.com", ARES_CLASS_IN, ARES_REC_TYPE_A,
                       QueryCallback, result, NULL);
